{"_meta":{"openai/outputTemplate":"ui://nooticr/mention_trend.html","ui":{"resourceUri":"ui://nooticr/mention_trend"},"ui/resourceUri":"ui://nooticr/mention_trend"},"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true},"description":"What a brand watch has SEEN OVER TIME, from the history of its scheduled runs. Use when the question is how mentions or a competitor's median changed across runs, not what is being said now. Takes `watchId` (or `term`) and an optional `days`. Returns one point per run: when it ran, how many mentions it found, how many were new, and both counts per network \u2014 so \"which network is growing\" and \"did it go quiet, or did we stop looking\" are separable. On a competitor watch each point also carries the median that run measured, which is what turns \"they beat their own median\" into \"and that median has doubled\". Also returns the mentions more than one run has seen. No cost to call: the sweeps were billed when they ran. Read the series yourself and say what changed \u2014 this returns numbers, not a verdict.","execution":{"taskSupport":"forbidden"},"inputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"days":{"description":"Window in days (default 90). Clamped to how long the backend keeps runs, which comes back as `retainedDays` \u2014 asking for more silently returns less, and a flat start would read as silence rather than as the edge of the record.","type":"integer"},"term":{"description":"The watched term, if you do not have the id. One of the two is required.","type":"string"},"watchId":{"description":"The watch id from list_brand_watches.","type":"string"}},"type":"object"},"name":"mention_trend","outputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","additionalProperties":true,"properties":{"available":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"number"},{"type":"boolean"},{"type":"null"}]},"billable":{"anyOf":[{"ty